1
00:00:00,029 --> 00:00:03,480
Open Calls and choose the
community care check-in exercise.

2
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:07,530
Confirm its training title and department
call number before you continue.

3
00:00:08,199 --> 00:00:12,920
The left panel identifies Engine
51, the apparatus selected in Unit.

4
00:00:13,340 --> 00:00:17,940
No Active Call means that opening a
call to read it has not itself assigned

5
00:00:17,940 --> 00:00:19,790
that call as the unit's response.

6
00:00:20,229 --> 00:00:23,399
This example uses a fictional
community paramedicine and

7
00:00:23,399 --> 00:00:24,829
mental health outreach visit.

8
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:28,360
The same check-in tools can
support other department workflows.

9
00:00:28,589 --> 00:00:30,740
In Call Details, open Check-In.

10
00:00:31,329 --> 00:00:34,679
The Personnel card shows the
check-in type, the time since the

11
00:00:34,679 --> 00:00:36,980
last entry, and its current state.

12
00:00:37,410 --> 00:00:41,490
Here the last check-in was ten
minutes ago, the counter reads ten of

13
00:00:41,490 --> 00:00:44,080
sixty minutes, and the state is OK.

14
00:00:44,490 --> 00:00:48,060
These values help a coordinator
see when a scheduled update is due.

15
00:00:48,469 --> 00:00:52,639
The sixty-minute interval comes from
department configuration; it is not a

16
00:00:52,639 --> 00:00:54,750
duration that the crew sets on this card.

17
00:00:54,909 --> 00:00:56,830
Open History below the timer.

18
00:00:57,270 --> 00:01:01,379
The saved Personnel entry includes
its timestamp and note, so you can

19
00:01:01,379 --> 00:01:04,840
distinguish an earlier check-in from
an update you are about to enter.

20
00:01:05,270 --> 00:01:09,119
In this exercise the note identifies
a scheduled software check-in

21
00:01:09,119 --> 00:01:10,510
for the community care visit.

22
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:14,689
Check the history before repeating
an update, especially when a crew

23
00:01:14,689 --> 00:01:17,779
changes or another team member
may already have checked in.

24
00:01:18,220 --> 00:01:22,320
A saved software entry does not
establish someone's physical location.

25
00:01:22,479 --> 00:01:24,729
Select Check In on the Personnel card.

26
00:01:25,190 --> 00:01:29,550
In the form, confirm Personnel
under Select check-in type, then

27
00:01:29,550 --> 00:01:31,830
use Add note to explain the update.

28
00:01:32,190 --> 00:01:36,400
Our note says this is a follow-up
software check-in after reviewing history.

29
00:01:36,809 --> 00:01:39,410
Review the wording and
select Confirm Check-In.

30
00:01:39,949 --> 00:01:43,590
Use a short, useful note that
follows your department's procedures.

31
00:01:43,850 --> 00:01:47,350
For search and rescue or security
patrols, describe the agreed

32
00:01:47,350 --> 00:01:50,979
reporting update without adding
unnecessary personal details.

33
00:01:51,190 --> 00:01:54,229
After confirmation, review
the Personnel card again.

34
00:01:54,639 --> 00:01:59,149
The displayed age is now zero minutes,
the counter reads zero of sixty

35
00:01:59,149 --> 00:02:01,630
minutes, and the state remains OK.

36
00:02:02,059 --> 00:02:04,239
This is the observed
reset for this check-in.

37
00:02:04,890 --> 00:02:08,820
A timer reset and a unit status
change are separate operations.

38
00:02:09,220 --> 00:02:12,839
Wildland contractors and industrial
response teams can use the same

39
00:02:12,839 --> 00:02:16,669
distinction when coordinating regular
reports during a longer assignment.

40
00:02:16,829 --> 00:02:19,470
Open History again and
read the newest entry.

41
00:02:19,899 --> 00:02:22,609
The follow-up note appears
above the earlier scheduled

42
00:02:22,609 --> 00:02:24,569
check-in, with its own timestamp.

43
00:02:25,060 --> 00:02:27,869
This is how you verify that
the note was stored, rather

44
00:02:27,869 --> 00:02:29,409
than simply left in the form.

45
00:02:29,860 --> 00:02:33,070
Check both the timer and history
when learning this workflow.

46
00:02:33,519 --> 00:02:37,240
Your department decides the reporting
interval and escalation procedure;

47
00:02:37,599 --> 00:02:41,250
the app supplies the check-in
controls and a record of the updates.

